{
  "_comment": "Same model combo as truth_richer.json (softbroken SN colour, linear mass, tanh sSFR, gamma_alpha), but with alpha/beta/Om0 switched from informative truncated_gaussian priors to uniform over the same hard range -- isolates how much of any richer-model recovery bias/scatter comes from those three informative priors vs. genuine data/model-structure effects. Compare seed-by-seed against truth_richer.json runs.",

  "model": {
    "sn_colour":     "softbroken",
    "x1_correction": "linear",
